# tree_diameter:
# CSES 1131, Tree Diameter (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1131), in our own words: a
# tree of n nodes, numbered 1 to n, given by its n - 1 edges, each joining two nodes;
# the diameter, the greatest number of edges on the path between two nodes. The input
# is the binary natural n (corpora/library/binary/natural), at least 1, and the edges,
# a Scott list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of pairs `pair a b`
# (corpora/library/prelude/pair) of binary naturals from 1 to n, which make a tree;
# the answer is a binary natural. Part of the CSES port's fourth batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: node b is reached from node a within steps
# edges when a = b, or when some edge joins a to a node that reaches b within one step
# fewer (steps 0 allows no edge); the distance of two nodes is the least steps within
# which the first reaches the second, which is below n since a path repeats no node
# (the search answers n + 1 past n, which no tree reaches); the diameter is the
# greatest distance over every pair of nodes. Under tabling the reading shares the
# reachability for each steps and pair of nodes, about n cubed times the edges; the
# replacement the family asks for is two breadth-first searches, the first from any
# node to its farthest node, the second from that node to its farthest, in about n
# steps, on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since reaches consumes
# steps, a binary numeral that falls by one at each call, the search for a distance
# consumes the gap n - steps, the two loops over the nodes consume the gap n - node,
# and every other recursion consumes a finite list; the branches that a Scott boolean
# discards are never read. binary_subtract, which writes no top
# (../common/binary_modular), is asked for steps - 1 only when steps is not zero. So
# ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of the derivable equations for the
# contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an answer, P
# ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while Böhm's
# theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and applying
# both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than binary_maximum _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ _ binary_subtract _ _
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_odd binary_zero))
λ one
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ edges
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self steps from target
        . merge_binary_equality from target true
          ( ( λ any
              . steps false (λ_. any edges) λ_. any edges
            )
            ( fixpoint
              ( λ walk rest
                . rest false
                  λ edge others
                  . edge
                    λ left right
                    . (merge_binary_equality from left (self (binary_subtract steps one false) right target) false)
                      true
                      ( (merge_binary_equality from right (self (binary_subtract steps one false) left target) false)
                        true (walk others)
                      )
              )
            )
          )
      )
  )
λ reaches
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ node_count edges
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self steps from target
        . binary_less_than node_count steps (merge_binary_increment node_count)
          (reaches edges steps from target steps (self (merge_binary_increment steps) from target))
      ) binary_zero
  )
λ distance
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ node_count edges from
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self target most
        . binary_less_than node_count target most
          (self (merge_binary_increment target) (binary_maximum most (distance node_count edges from target)))
      ) one binary_zero
  )
λ farthest
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ node_count edges
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self from most
        . binary_less_than node_count from most
          (self (merge_binary_increment from) (binary_maximum most (farthest node_count edges from)))
      ) one binary_zero
  )
λ tree_diameter
. export tree_diameter
